# Impeccable design skill.
# The engine is a ~12MB prebuilt binary, one copy per agent directory, and it
# is per-platform (darwin-arm64 here, useless to anyone on Linux). It is never
# built locally: `pnpm skills:update` downloads it, and failing that the
# committed `scripts/impeccable` launcher fetches the release matching its
# `VERSION` file, checks it against the published sha256, and caches it in
# ~/.impeccable/bin/<version>/ on first use. So a clone without it self-heals.
**/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/

# Decisions are shared and committed: config.json (team workflow config),
# design.json (the DESIGN.md sidecar), live/config.json (injection shape),
# critique/ignore.md (shared suppressions). Everything below is per-machine
# runtime state or regenerable output from a single run.
.impeccable/config.local.json
.impeccable/live/sessions/
.impeccable/live/inject-journal.json
.impeccable/live/roots.json
.impeccable/build/
.impeccable/mocks/
.impeccable/review/
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
